 {"id": "PERF-OFF-BY-ONE-1", "title": "[P3] seed's install step pays a per-statement fsync: 44.7-70.5s on ext4 vs 3.4-3.7s on tmpfs for the same corpus and binary (17x) \u2014 not the link scan", "status": "complete", "priority": "P3", "complexity": 2, "type": "task", "created_by": "dogfood-off-by-one-2026-10-23-1243b", "created_at": "2026-10-23T13:06:33Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-23T19:00:00Z", "capability_tags": ["perf", "sqlite", "seed", "install"], "reasoning": "Measured on the RELEASED v0.2.0 artifact (asset sha256 c2638ce9\u2026a013fc) against a depth-1 clone of HEAD ea5b963a, host /tmp on /dev/nvme0n1p2 (ext4), corpus = data/answers/*.json (2856 files).\n\nEXACT COMMAND (control and treatment are the same command; only the -db target differs):\n  /usr/bin/time -f 'WALL=%e user=%U sys=%S' ../off-by-one-v0.2.0-linux-amd64 seed -db <DB>\n\next4 arm: 44.70s (user 6.06 sys 1.31) \u00b7 59.53s (6.53/1.43) \u00b7 64.21s (6.81/1.41) \u00b7 70.51s under strace (9.88/11.17)\ntmpfs arm (-db /dev/shm/<fresh>.db): 3.72s (3.41/0.40) \u00b7 3.39s (3.10/0.39)\nEvery arm prints the identical result line: files=2856; classes=2856 created / 0 existing; answers=2955 created / 1530 skipped; edges=12872 created.\n\u21d2 17x wall difference, ~56s of it added by disk writes. CPU is the SAME work in both arms (~3.4s tmpfs vs ~8.2s ext4), so the per-class link scan cannot own the seconds: that scan runs in BOTH arms.\n\nSyscall census (strace -f -c on an ext4 arm): 9136 fsync, 253070 pwrite64, 130177 nanosleep, 29361 futex, 3208 tgkill \u2014 top entry futex 36.95s.\n\nHot path (read-only inspection, no code changed):\n- internal/seed/seed.go:91 \u2014 `for _, ent := range entries { seedFile(...) }`; internal/seed/seed.go:127 calls store.UpsertProblemClass per file.\n- `grep -c -E 'Begin|Commit' internal/seed/seed.go` = 0 \u2014 no transaction wraps the load, so every INSERT autocommits.\n- internal/graph/store.go:152 \u2014 DSN `_pragma=journal_mode(WAL)&_pragma=busy_timeout(5000)`; each autocommitted statement in WAL pays its own fsync.\n- internal/graph/linker.go \u2014 LinkAllSimilar writes one INSERT per edge (12872 edges) through the same autocommit path.\n\nUser impact: this is the headline install step of README \"Install from a release\"; the user waits ~1 minute for ~4s of work before the catalog exists, and the README's \"zero to a working catalog in under a minute\" claim then depends on host I/O luck (measured envelopes on this box: 52s with the 44.7s seed; >70s with the 64-70s seeds).\n\nRelationship to the earlier dogfood entry for this tick (docs/dogfood/2026-10-23-release-artifact-integration.md \u00a7Performance): its numbers are reproduced here (it recorded 58.97s) but its ATTRIBUTION is not \u2014 it assigned the residual to \"the per-class link scan already tracked as OB-GAP-073\" and concluded \"nothing a user would feel\". OB-GAP-073 is closed, and the tmpfs control shows the link scan is not the cost; the cost is per-statement fsync on the install path. A one-minute first-install wait is user-noticeable, so this is filed as a PERF row rather than left as a note.\n\nFix shape (foreman's call): wrap the whole seed load (classes + answers + edges, including LinkAllSimilar) in ONE transaction, or in per-chunk batches with a single fsync each; keep the loader idempotent. Expected: ext4 seed lands in the tmpfs arm's 3-4s range; fsync count drops from 9136 to a handful.", "acceptance_criteria": "A fresh seed on the same corpus and binary completes in <=10s wall on ext4: `/usr/bin/time -f 'WALL=%e user=%U sys=%S' ./off-by-one seed -db /tmp/seed-perf-a.db` (fresh DB path) reports WALL <= 10, against the recorded baseline 44.70/59.53/64.21/70.51s and the tmpfs control 3.39/3.72s; the post-fix ext4 arm must land within ~1s of the same command run with -db /dev/shm/seed-perf-b.db.\n\nThe fsync count drops by two orders of magnitude: `strace -f -c -o /tmp/seed-perf.strace ./off-by-one seed -db /tmp/seed-perf-c.db` then `grep fsync /tmp/seed-perf.strace` shows fewer than 100 calls (recorded baseline: 9136 fsync, 253070 pwrite64).\n\nLoader output and idempotency are unchanged: a fresh DB prints `files=2856; classes=2856 created / 0 existing; answers=2955 created / 1530 skipped; edges=12872 created`, and a second `seed` on that same DB prints classes `0 created / 2856 existing` with the same answer/edge totals.\n\nNo unit regression: `go test ./internal/seed/... ./internal/graph/...` PASS at the fixing commit.\n\nThe completion note must quote the measured WALL and fsync numbers from criteria 1-2 (not a description of the change).", "detail": {"fingerprint": "c298508ad1a351fa1cc00e287bf0e0cc9891df8a616d1c7a74393f3f3f29006e", "evidence": [{"run_id": "perf-seed-fsync-2026-10-23", "ts": "2026-10-23T13:06:33Z"}]}, "worker_status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-10-23T19:00:00Z", "attempts": 1, "exit_code": 0, "commit_hash": "27605bb013bbcb2cf3a38077ea49953eb471d25e", "files_changed": ["internal/graph/batch.go", "internal/graph/batch_test.go", "internal/graph/store.go", "internal/seed/seed.go", "internal/seed/seed_batch_test.go"], "lines_added": 623, "lines_removed": 21, "guard_result": "PASS: gitreins guard Tier 1 secrets clean; build/tests verified separately", "ci_result": "3 recent GitHub Actions runs completed success before tick", "worker_summary": "Implemented one-transaction corpus seed batching with filesystem parse phase outside the transaction; added graph Tx and atomic/idempotency tests. Commit 27605bb0. Internal seed/graph tests, full short suite, build, vet, and guard passed. Live judge e839da35 tier1+tier2 PASS: ext4 fresh seed 7.28s, 29 fsyncs, output files=2860/classes=2860/answers=2959/edges=12890; rerun classes 0/2860 existing, answers 0/4489 skipped, edges 0. ch:trace row=PERF-OFF-BY-ONE-1 spec=.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl#PERF-OFF-BY-ONE-1 wave=none:serial-tick test=internal/seed/seed_batch_test.go::TestSeedAtomicRollbackOnWriteError doc=none:code-performance-task prompt=/tmp